Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:15:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1001/1002] SableOS: pure Files keyboard model

The Sable Files key model (FILES_DOCUMENTS_UX "Keyboard model") for a
keyboard with Alt, Shift and Sym but no Ctrl or Fn key, such as the
Zinwa Q25.

Letters keep their upstream meaning, type-to-focus (typing a name moves
focus to it; Enter opens, Space previews). The design's single-letter
commands therefore take Alt, the key this keyboard has instead of Ctrl
or Fn:

* Alt+C Copy to..., Alt+M Move to... (both pick a visible destination
  first), Alt+R rename, Alt+N new folder, Alt+I info, Alt+O open with,
  Alt+A select all.
* "/" (Alt+G on the Q25) opens search.
* Del deletes the selection or the focused file, after the upstream
  confirmation; with nothing selected or focused it keeps going up one
  folder.

On the Q25 Alt+letter also types a symbol or digit, so the other Alt
keys keep feeding type-to-focus, and while a type-to-focus search runs
every key belongs to it. Nothing fires while a text field has focus;
Ctrl and Meta chords keep their upstream meaning.

Pure Java (sable/SableFilesKeys.java); host tests live in the SableOS
Q25 repository under tests/java/stock-apps/DocumentsUI.
